::: moniker range="vs-2019"

Jak tworzyć kontrakty dotyczące testów jednostkowych i testować kod C# przy użyciu ramki Pex.

## <a name="prerequisites"></a>Wymagania wstępne

- Dostęp do subskrypcji programu Visual Studio albo programu Visual Studio Enterprise. 
- Microsoft Fakes i Microsoft System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis.DynamicCodeAnalysis for .NET - zainstalowane w wersji Enterprise-
- Platforma testowania wspólnego (CTP) dla wersji 16,3, zainstalowana w systemie Windows 10

Teraz, przejdźmy do przesłoniania niektórych przypadków użycia.--------------------
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= index || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX < index);

	    // ensure your assertions should also ensure that the insertion  at the proper index

           Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX == index);
        }
    }
}

In the above test case, the assumptions are:

1. The index being added is less than or equal to the current size of the array list, and greater than or equal to zero.

2. The index is a correct index for the array list, meaning it’s between 0 and count (not inclusive). 

The tests observe, observe the current size, and index of the element, and if it is found. Then, the test asserts that the element index is within the array list’s size and found elements are found at the specified index. Also, it checks whether the last index isn’t less than the given index, indicating the presence of the element after the expected position. 

The contract test might require adding more tests because the contract specifies that insertion at a proper index should work and the last position of inserted element won't be before last specified position. Thus, the contract should be fulfilled by the insertion and the presence of element after the last specified position.

This contract should indeed make inserting an element at the specific index in the array-like structure possible. It defines a state where the inserted element exists in the list, in the proper place and all previous elements are found before it. The tests should verify this. That’s why the contract's assumptions and assertions must be carefully defined for an effective testing.

As always, more complex contracts could be tested with more comprehensive specifications, especially when testing complex collection types like 'ArrayList'.
            














            

            
            

            


            

            
            
            
            
            
            

    

            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            


            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
            

            
            
            
            


            
            
            
            
            
            
      --------------------            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_index);

            // check count and new x's position
            Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount + 1, New_arrListCount);
            Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, Old_index);
            Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX);
            Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListLastIndexOfX, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
        }
    }
}

//List-Test/ArrayList.Test/TestSources/ArrayListContractTest.cs
﻿using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Ranges;
using NUnit.Framework;
using System.Collections;
using ArrayList.Test;

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    [TestFixture]
    [PexClass(typeof(ArrayList))]
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        [PexMethod]
        public void AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            arrList.Add(x);
            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

            Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount + 1, New_arrListCount);
        }
    }
}

